    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math learning by adapting to individual student needs, providing step-by-step explanations for difficult topics, and generating practice problems tailored to a student’s level. They can also help teachers create engaging materials and clarify misconceptions in real time, making math more accessible and less intimidating."
